{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full; the disputed fee is held rather than collected or refunded while the review is pending."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: this ruling does not refund the no-show fee, and to the driver: it does not pay your compensation either — the case now goes to a human reviewer, and the SGD 4.00 fee is held rather than collected or refunded while that review is pending.\n\nOn the trip itself, the record supports the fee. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold: the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 09:30:20; the GPS trace puts the driver about 24 m from the pickup pin — well inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius — from the first fix at 09:30:00, i.e. before that event (POL-NS-02); the driver held position for one continuous 330-second run, exceeding the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum, measured from the first in-geofence fix rather than the 'arrived' tap; and the trip was ended by the driver at 09:35:30 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell elapsed at 09:35:00. The fare breakdown's SGD 4.00 line reconciles with the fee schedule (the greater of the SGD 4.00 zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X tier fee), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) price defect, and no clock-skew, trace-gap or chat-truncation impairment under POL-NS-08(a)-(c).\n\nThe rider's exoneration routes do not open. POL-NS-04 fails at limb (a): the only two chat messages are the system 'driver has arrived' notice and the driver's own 'Waiting at PLQ 3 pickup bay' — the rider sent nothing locating or coordinating — and limb (c) fails affirmatively, all 16 rider fixes sitting about 519 m from the pin, outside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius. POL-NS-05 does not bite: at the arrival marker the driver was ~24 m from the pin and stationary at 0.0 km/h. POL-NS-06 does not bite: there is no shortfall (330 s against 300 s). The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09108-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, and can carry no fact, so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation could not be run in any event — and it changes nothing, because the minimum dwell was met.\n\nThe case turns on the driver's compensation. POL-NS-07 would ordinarily pay 80 percent of the fee, SGD 3.20, but its anti-farming check trips on both limbs: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more) and 7 divided by completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, above the 0.08 rate threshold. Compensation is therefore withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). Escalation replaces any money ruling, so no amount is refunded to the rider now and no payment is made to the driver; the fee is held. This is not a rider win, only a pause.\n\nFor the reviewer: the open question is whether this driver's 30-day termination pattern is genuine fee-farming rather than ordinary high volume. POL-NS-07 directs that the escalation packet instruct you to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full, and that instruction is recorded in the referrals. Every rider-side abuse indicator is negative (no_show_disputes_30d 0, and disputes_with_counterparty_90d 0 on both sides), and under POL-GEN-01 the rider's prior_no_show_flags is a context-only lifetime counter that may not be used against her, so no adverse finding rests on her profile."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the anti-farming check has tripped on this driver, so the escalation packet must direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full if the pattern is confirmed on review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: on the trip itself the record is clear and both sides effectively agree on it, but this case cannot be closed by the automated pipeline.\n\nThe SGD 4.00 no-show fee was validly incurred. POL-NS-01 requires four things and all four are present. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 2026-09-08 09:30:20. (b) The GPS trace places him 24 m from the pickup pin from the first fix at 09:30:00, well inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup. (c) He then held position for one continuous qualifying run of 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum for LARGE_VENUE, measured from the first in-geofence fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 09:35:30 on cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, a code limb (d) recognises, after the dwell had elapsed at 09:35:00. POL-NS-02 independently confirms arrival (34 consecutive in-radius fixes, mean distance 24.0 m, no accuracy-filtering problem and no clock skew).\n\nNothing displaces the fee. POL-NS-05 does not bite: at the arrived timestamp the driver was 24 m from the pin, not more than 300 m, and the trace records a single distinct speed of 0.0 km/h, so the arrival marker is genuine and the waiting clock is not recomputed. POL-NS-06 does not bite: the effective dwell of 330 seconds exceeds the minimum by 30 seconds (shortfall_sec -30.0), so there is no waiting-period shortfall and no premature cancellation. POL-NS-03 has no purchase: it governs a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, whereas this driver was inside the arrival radius throughout, so there is no wrong-face-of-the-venue question. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: limb (a) fails because the only two chat entries are the system arrival notice and the driver's own 'Waiting at PLQ 3 pickup bay' — the rider sent nothing locating or coordinating — and limb (c) fails affirmatively, with her device's 16 fixes at a mean 519 m from the pin, outside the 150 m rider-presence radius, and 0 qualifying fixes. The amount also reconciles under POL-NS-08(d): the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is exactly the SGD 4.00 cancellation line on the fare breakdown, and no other fare defect appears.\n\nThe rider's refund demand is therefore not supported on the merits of this trip. But the driver does not collect either. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the fee — SGD 3.20 — only where its anti-farming check is clear, and on this driver it is not: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, above the 0.08 rate. The two limbs are conjunctive and both are met, so compensation is withheld and POL-NS-09(d) requires the case to go to a human reviewer. Escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal: the automated pipeline issues no monetary ruling in either direction, and the disputed SGD 4.00 stays at payment_status PENDING — held, not collected and not refunded — while review is pending. The escalation packet carries the instruction POL-NS-07 directs into it: if the pattern is confirmed, the reviewer must refund the rider's cancellation fee in full.\n\nOne further point of record: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09108-01 is MISSING, carries no payload, fires MISSING_ARTIFACT and has weight_multiplier 0.0, so under POL-GEN-02 it can carry no fact and POL-NS-06(i) cannot be run to accumulate any additional in-geofence time. That makes no difference to this case, because the measured dwell already clears the minimum. All artifacts carrying the deciding facts (trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown, driver profile) sit at weight 1.0, so no discount applies to the confidence in this ruling.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: whether the driver's 7 no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days reflect genuine rider no-shows or fee-farming. If they are genuine, the SGD 4.00 fee stands and the question of the SGD 3.20 compensation returns; if they are not, the rider's fee is refunded in full as the packet instructs."
  },
